{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4717",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, both of which are subunits of the Nadh dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) complex, and Ndufc1 is a subunit of the same complex. This suggests that Metformin may modulate the activity of the Nadh dehydrogenase complex, which is involved in mitochondrial respiration. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent mechanism by which Metformin influences the activity of the complex, leading to a potential role in Ndufc1 regulation. The high scores in all three paths suggest a strong and reliable interaction, supported by multiple independent pathways. The mechanism involves Metformin binding to subunits of the complex, which in turn affects the overall activity of the complex, potentially influencing Ndufc1. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple overlapping pathways, reinforcing the biological plausibility of the interaction. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Metformin may exert its effects through modulation of the Nadh dehydrogenase complex, with Ndufc1 being a key component in this process.",
